.TH RFINDD 8 "2026-10-14" "rfind 1.0.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
rfindd \- filesystem indexing daemon for rfind
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rfindd
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rfindd
builds and maintains the index searched by
.BR rfind (1):
the name, type, size and modification time of every file and directory
under the configured roots, stored in an SQLite database.
It runs as root, normally as the systemd service
.BR rfindd.service ,
and logs to standard error (the journal).
.SS Scanning
The first start scans every live root with a parallel scanner that reads
directories with
.BR getdents64 (2)
and collects metadata with
.BR statx (2),
batched through
.BR io_uring (7)
when the kernel allows it.
Scans never empty the index: each one upserts the entries it sees and then
deletes the entries under its root that it didn't see, so searches keep
returning complete results while a scan runs.
.SS Live updates
Changes are reported by the kernel and applied within about five seconds:
.TP
.B fanotify
(preferred; Linux 5.9 or newer, root): one mark per filesystem covers
everything on it, with no per-directory watches.
Renames arrive as single events on Linux 5.17 or newer.
.TP
.B inotify
(fallback): one watch per directory, registered before each directory is
read so nothing is missed between listing and watching.
.TP
.B index-only
(neither available): live roots are rescanned every
.B reindex_interval_hours
hours.
.PP
Events are first written to a journal in the database and then applied by
re-checking each path on disk, so a crash or a replay never corrupts the
index.
If the kernel's event queue overflows, the live roots are rescanned.
.SS Periodic roots
Roots listed as periodic (see
.BR rfind.conf (5))
are rescanned in a background thread on their own interval and never
monitored.
This suits filesystems whose changes the kernel can't report: Windows
drives under WSL2 (changes made from Windows produce no events) and network
shares (changes made by other clients don't either).
.SS Mounts
Bind mounts that show files already indexed through another mount point
(WSL2's
.IR /mnt/wslg/distro ,
container volumes) are detected from
.I /proc/self/mountinfo
and skipped.
With
.B monitor.watch_new_mounts
(default on), filesystems mounted under a live root after startup are
indexed and watched, and the mount point of an unmounted filesystem is
rescanned.
rfindd never keeps files open on marked filesystems, so they can be
unmounted normally.
.SS Restarts
On restart rfindd replays the journal instead of rescanning when the last
full scan is younger than
.BR reindex_interval_hours .
If the configuration changed, it removes entries that are now excluded or
outside every root and rescans the live roots; periodic roots are rescanned
only if something inside them stopped being excluded.
An index written by an incompatible version is rebuilt from scratch.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload the configuration: running scans are cancelled and rfindd
re-executes itself (keeping its PID) with the new configuration.
An invalid configuration is reported and ignored.
.RB "Sent by " "rfind reload" ", " "rfind config" " and " "systemctl reload rfindd" .
.TP
.B SIGUSR1
Rescan the live roots now and schedule the periodic roots.
Signals arriving during that rescan are merged into it.
.RB "Sent by " "rfind update" .
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT
Stop: running scans are cancelled and the daemon exits within a second.
.SH SECURITY
The index lists every file name on the system, including other users'.
rfindd runs with umask 077, keeps
.I /var/lib/rfindd
at mode 0700 and the database at 0600, so only root can search.
Searching opens the database read-only.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RFIND_CONFIG
Configuration file to use instead of
.IR /etc/rfindd/config.toml .
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log level filter, e.g.
.BR debug .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/rfindd/config.toml
Configuration, written with defaults on first start; see
.BR rfind.conf (5).
.TP
.I /var/lib/rfindd/index.db
The index, with its
.I \-wal
and
.I \-shm
files.
With
.B index.compress
(the default) this file is an empty stub that carries SQLite's locks; the
pages are stored zstd-compressed in
.I index.db\-zdata.N
with a page map in
.IR index.db\-zmap .
.TP
.I /run/rfindd/progress.json
Current phase and scan progress.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/rfindd.service
The service unit installed by
.IR scripts/install.sh .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 after a clean shutdown; 1 if the configuration is invalid or the index
can't be opened.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rfind (1),
.BR rfind.conf (5),
.BR fanotify (7),
.BR inotify (7),
.BR io_uring (7),
.BR systemctl (1)
.PP
https://github.com/YanivSaar/rfind
